"**Summary**\n\n**a. Verdict**  \nI have proved that the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is  \n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,\\,n-2\\}} .\n\\]\n\n**b. Method Sketch**  \n1. **Lower bound** \u2013 show that \\(k=0\\) is attainable by taking the \\(n\\) vertical lines \\(x=1,\\dots ,x=n\\).  \n2. **Upper bound** \u2013 prove that in any family of \\(n\\) distinct lines covering all points \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a,b\\ge 1\\) and \\(a+b\\le n+1\\) at least two of the lines must be parallel to one of the three forbidden directions (the \\(x\\)-axis, the \\(y\\)-axis or the line \\(x+y=0\\)). Hence at most \\(n-2\\) lines can be sunny.  \n3. **Realisation of every intermediate value** \u2013 for each \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\) construct a family of \\(n\\) lines containing exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.  \n   * Use two vertical lines \\(x=1\\) and \\(x=n\\) (non\u2011sunny).  \n   * For the remaining \\(n-2\\) lines, choose \\(k\\) of them to be sunny, each passing through a distinct point \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a+b\\le n+1\\) and not parallel to any forbidden direction; the other \\(n-2-k\\) lines are taken to be horizontal (also non\u2011sunny).  \n   * Verify that every lattice point of the triangle is covered by at least one of the constructed lines.\n\nThe combination of the upper bound and the explicit constructions shows that the admissible values of \\(k\\) are precisely the integers from \\(0\\) up to \\(n-2\\).\n\n---\n\n**Detailed Solution**\n\nLet  \n\n\\[\nT_n=\\{(a,b)\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge 1}^2\\mid a+b\\le n+1\\}\n\\]\n\nbe the set of lattice points that have to lie on at least one of the \\(n\\) lines.\nA line is called **sunny** if its direction is different from the three forbidden\ndirections: horizontal \\((\\text{slope }0)\\), vertical \\((\\text{slope }\\infty)\\) and slope \\(-1\\) (the line \\(x+y=0\\)).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 1.  Existence of a configuration with \\(k=0\\)\n\nTake the \\(n\\)